"Predicate" and "relation" are interchangeable, roughly. (There's a formal
nitpick about a "relation" which has only one argument, but that's not
really very interesting or important.) Anyway, "predicate relationship",
"predication", and "proposition" are examples of English words similar to
the x1 of bridi. "Predicate" is not.

mu'o mi'e .latros.

