> Well, it's certainly odd that the definitions are listed like that, but
> they are all based on the same word, bridi. {selbri} is {se bridi}, {terbri}
> is {te bridi}. In the lojban "sentence" {mi klama lo do zdani fu lo karce}
> ("I go to your house in my car."), "mi klama lo do zdani fu lo karce" is a
> bridi (a predicate), "klama" is a selbri (a relation), and "mi", "lo do
> zdani", and "lo karce" are terbri (a relationship argument).
